<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Federated States of Micronesia</h1><p class="st-meta">1986 CE – present · capital Palikir</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A federation of four Caroline Island states (Yap, Chuuk, Pohnpei and Kosrae), independent in free association with the United States since 1986.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The islands belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trust-territory-of-the-pacific-islands">Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands</a>, administered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> from 1947. On 10 May 1979 four of its districts ratified a constitution to become the Federated States of Micronesia. The Compact of Free Association entered into force on 3 November 1986, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> ended the trusteeship in 1990.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The 1979 constitution guarantees fundamental rights and sets up a unicameral Congress of fourteen members, which elects the president and vice president from among its four state senators. There are no formal political parties. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> is wholly responsible for defence, and the Compact lets citizens join the US military and work in the United States. The country joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> in 1991. Economic activity is mainly subsistence farming and fishing, and aid from the United States is the main source of revenue.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The Compact was renewed in 2004. In February 2021, after a leadership dispute, the Federated States announced it would leave the Pacific Islands Forum, but in June 2022 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suva">Suva</a> Agreement was reached and it agreed to remain. In February 2022 it ended diplomatic relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/federated-states-of-micronesia.jpg" alt="Federated States of Micronesia" width="330" height="174"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Federated_States_of_Micronesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1986 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Palikir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christian (Catholic Church, Protestant churches)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, with local languages in each state</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Federated States of Micronesia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Micronesia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2006&amp;focus=federated-states-of-micronesia" aria-label="Federated States of Micronesia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="9059 1919 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Federated States of Micronesia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M9379 2175L9188 2042"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M9188 2042h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M9379 2175h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M9379 2175h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Palikir. <a href="/atlas?year=2006&amp;focus=federated-states-of-micronesia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
